THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because `getPredNodeNumbers` returns the possibly-null result of `predecessors.getRelated(...)` while its return type is non-null `IntSet`. The analogous `getSuccNodeNumbers` method already handles null by returning `EmptyIntSet.instance`. I should mirror that pattern for predecessors. I’ll edit the file to introduce a local variable, check for null, and return `EmptyIntSet.instance` when appropriate, then run the build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/wala-util && sed -i '143,149s/@Override/@Override
  public IntSet getPredNodeNumbers(T node) throws IllegalArgumentException {
    if (nodeManager.getNumber(node) < 0) {
      throw new IllegalArgumentException("Node not in graph " + node);
    }
    IntSet x = predecessors.getRelated(nodeManager.getNumber(node));
    if (x == null) {
      return EmptyIntSet.instance;
    } else {
      return x;
    }
  }

  @Override/' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/graph/impl/SparseNumberedEdgeManager.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5 || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

